# Compose-level env for Daimon (docker-compose.yml). Copy to .env only if you need to
# override; everything here runs without it. Hermes runtime secrets are separate —
# see config/.env.example (seeded into ~/.hermes/.env).

# Optional OpenAI key for the fallback model — the only runtime secret compose passes
# through, so you can keep it next to the rest of your local config instead of editing
# ~/.hermes/.env inside the volume. Unset means Daimon runs local-only.
# OPENAI_PROFILE_API_KEY=

# The external Docker network your shared infra stack (Ollama/Redis/Qdrant/observability)
# runs on. Daimon and his sidecars join it to reach those services by DNS. Default: shared.
# SHARED_NETWORK=shared

# Miniflux (optional feeds source) is not part of Daimon: run your own, with its own
# admin credentials and Postgres. The `feeds` adapter consumes it via MINIFLUX_* in
# ~/.hermes/.env — see config/.env.example.
#
# Observability (Grafana/Loki/Prometheus + alerting → Telegram) lives on your shared
# stack too; its monitoring TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN / TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID alert vars belong there.
# The telemetry sidecars here (chat-shipper, status-exporter) need no env.
